      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoversouthernindiana.com/blog/post/5-reasons-to-visit-ireland-indiana/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Ireland Historical Society occupies the former 1878 Ireland Methodist Church, home to over 1,000 historic photographs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoversouthernindiana.com/blog/post/5-reasons-to-visit-ireland-indiana/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former Ireland Methodist Church also houses the Ireland Historical Chapel, preserving local heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoversouthernindiana.com/blog/post/5-reasons-to-visit-ireland-indiana/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Shiloh Meeting House, built in 1849, is one of Southern Indiana’s finest pioneer churches and is on the National Register.",
